 "title": "Temporal Standards",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h1",
   "text": "Temporal Standards"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Temporal is based on the following standards:"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Name",
     "Description"
    ],
    [
     "ISO 8601 Date/Time",
     "International standard"
    ],
    [
     "ISO 8601 Duration",
     "ISO 8601 duration codes"
    ],
    [
     "RFC 3339 Date/Time",
     "Internet standard"
    ],
    [
     "RFC 9557 Date/Time",
     "Temporal standard"
    ],
    [
     "RFC 5545 iCalendar",
     "The iCalendar data format"
    ],
    [
     "JavaScript Calendars",
     "Internet calendar systems"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The ISO 8601 Standard"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "ISO 8601 is the International Standard for representing dates and times."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "It is a machine-readable text format in the form YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ssZ."
  },
  {
   "type": "image",
   "src": "https://www.w3schools.com/jsref/img_iso8601.svg",
   "alt": "ISO 8601"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "ISO 8601 was designed to eliminate confusion caused by regional date variations."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "It follows a \"largest to smallest\" hierarchy (year, month, day, hour, minute, second)\nwhich ensures that dates are alphabetically sortable."
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Note"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "ISO 8601 avoids confusion between regional formats like:"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "MM/DD/YYYY (US format)",
    "DD/MM/YYYY (European format)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "ISO 8601 Strings"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "An ISO 8601 string represents dates and times in a structured and sortable format:"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Format",
     "Description"
    ],
    [
     "YYYY",
     "A 4-digit year"
    ],
    [
     "MM",
     "2-digit month"
    ],
    [
     "DD",
     "2-digit day"
    ],
    [
     "T",
     "Separator for time"
    ],
    [
     "hh",
     "Hour"
    ],
    [
     "mm",
     "Minute"
    ],
    [
     "ss",
     "Second"
    ],
    [
     "Z",
     "Zero (Zulu) time Zone"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Format",
     "Format",
     "Example"
    ],
    [
     "Date (4-digit year)",
     "YYYY-MM-DD",
     "2026-05-17"
    ],
    [
     "Time (24 hour)",
     "hh:mm:ss",
     "14:30:00"
    ],
    [
     "Date & Time",
     "YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ssZ",
     "2026-05-17T14:30:00Z"
    ],
    [
     "Date & Time UTC",
     "YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ssZ",
     "2026-05-17T14:30:00Z"
    ],
    [
     "Date & Time + Offset",
     "YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss±hh:mm",
     "2026-05-17T14:30:00+01:00"
    ],
    [
     "Week Date",
     "YYYY-Www-D",
     "2026-W20-7"
    ],
    [
     "Ordinal (001-366)",
     "YYYY-nnn",
     "2026-074"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "ISO 8601 Duration Codes"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "An ISO 8601 duration represent lengths of time."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "It uses a standard format starting with ±P (Period),\nfollowed by the structure nYnMnDTnHnMnS."
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Code",
     "Description"
    ],
    [
     "±",
     "Optional positive/negative duration (default is +)."
    ],
    [
     "P",
     "Duration designator (for period)"
    ],
    [
     "nY",
     "Number of calendar years"
    ],
    [
     "nM",
     "Number of calendar months"
    ],
    [
     "nW",
     "Number of weeks"
    ],
    [
     "nD",
     "Number of calendar days"
    ],
    [
     "T",
     "Time designator (precedes time components)"
    ],
    [
     "nH",
     "Number of hours"
    ],
    [
     "nM",
     "Number of minutes"
    ],
    [
     "nS",
     "Number of seconds"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "text",
   "text": "±P nY nM nW nD T nH nM nS",
   "caption": "Syntax"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "text",
   "text": "P3Y6M4DT12H30M5S",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "More Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Duration",
     "Code"
    ],
    [
     "1 Day",
     "P1D"
    ],
    [
     "45 Minutes",
     "PT45M"
    ],
    [
     "1 Year, 2 Months, 3 Days",
     "P1Y2M3D"
    ],
    [
     "4 Hours, 5 Minutes, 6 Seconds",
     "PT4H5M6S"
    ],
    [
     "2.5 Hours",
     "PT2H30M"
    ],
    [
     "5 Weeks",
     "P5W"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Usage Rules"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Time Separator\nIf you have hours, minutes, or seconds, you must use the T separator,\nor the code will be invalid (e.g. PT3H not P3H).",
    "Optionality\nComponents are optional, but at least one must be present after P or T.",
    "Order\nThe order must be preserved:\nP-> Y-> M-> W-> D-> T-> H-> M-> S.",
    "Decimal fractions\nYou can use decimal points for the smallest unit,\nlike PT0.0021S for 2.1 milliseconds."
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The RF 3339 Format"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "RFC 3339 is the Internet Standard for Date and Time Formats."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "It is a Subset of ISO 8601 designed for use in Internet protocols."
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Feature",
     "Description"
    ],
    [
     "Format",
     "Follows the ISO pattern YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ssZ"
    ],
    [
     "Time Zones",
     "Requires a Z for time zone UTC or an offset (+05:00)"
    ],
    [
     "T Separator",
     "Allows the \"T\" separator to be replaced by \" \" for readability"
    ],
    [
     "Web APIs",
     "The default format for timestamps in JSON and RESTful APIs"
    ],
    [
     "Programming",
     "Modern languages have bult-in support like toISOString()"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The RFC 9557 Format"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "RFC 9557 is the primary format used by JavaScript Temporal to represent dates."
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Feature",
     "ISO 8601",
     "RFC 3339",
     "RFC 9557"
    ],
    [
     "Format",
     "YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ssZ",
     "Same",
     "Same"
    ],
    [
     "UTC Offset",
     "Yes",
     "Yes",
     "Yes"
    ],
    [
     "IANA Zone",
     "No",
     "No",
     "[America/New_York]"
    ],
    [
     "Calendars",
     "ISO only",
     "ISO only",
     "[u-ca=hebrew]"
    ],
    [
     "Compabile",
     "The Standard",
     "Subset of ISO 8601",
     "Extends 3339"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "RFC 9557 was created because ISO 8601 and RFC 3339 did not contain enough\ninformation to determine the geographical time zone or handle future DST\n(Daylight Saving Time) changes."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "RFC 5545 iCalendar"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "RFC 5545 is the official internet standard for the iCalendar data format.\nIt defines how calendar systems should store and share calendar data like meetings, tasks,\nand free/busy times using plain text files."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "iCalendar is text-based. It Uses readable lines of text encoded in UTF-8."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "iCalendar is is application independent. It works across different apps like Apple Calendar,\nGoogle Calendar, and Microsoft Outlook."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "text",
   "text": "BEGIN:VCALENDAR\n\nVERSION:2.0\n\nPRODID:-//Example Corp//NONSGML Calendar App//EN\n\nCALSCALE:GREGORIAN\n\nMETHOD:PUBLISH\n\nBEGIN:VEVENT\n\nUID:uid123456789@example.com\n\nDTSTAMP:20260810T120000Z\n\nORGANIZER;CN=John Doe:mailto:john.doe@example.com\n\nDTSTART:20260812T140000Z\n\nDTEND:20260812T150000Z\n\nSUMMARY:Project Kickoff Meeting\n\nDESCRIPTION:Initial team synchronization and roadmap review.\n\nLOCATION:Conference Room A\n\nSTATUS:CONFIRMED\n\nCLASS:PUBLIC\n\nEND:VEVENT\n\nEND:VCALENDAR",
   "caption": "Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Field",
     "Description"
    ],
    [
     "BEGIN:VCALENDAR",
     "Required. Begins a calendar object."
    ],
    [
     "VERSION:2.0",
     "Required. Specifies compliance with RFC 5545."
    ],
    [
     "PRODID",
     "Required. -//Organization//Product//Language."
    ],
    [
     "BEGIN:VEVENT",
     "Required. Begins a single calendar event."
    ],
    [
     "UID",
     "A globally unique event identifier to prevent duplicates."
    ],
    [
     "DTSTAMP",
     "The exact date and time the file was generated."
    ],
    [
     "ORGANIZER",
     "Defines who is hosting or managing the event."
    ],
    [
     "DTSTART",
     "Event start time (YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ in UTC)."
    ],
    [
     "DTEND",
     "Event end time (YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ in UTC)."
    ],
    [
     "SUMMARY",
     "The title of the calendar event."
    ],
    [
     "DESCRIPTION",
     "The detailed notes or body text of the event."
    ],
    [
     "LOCATION",
     "The location of the event."
    ],
    [
     "CLASS",
     "PUBLIC, PRIVATE or CONFIDENTIAL."
    ],
    [
     "STATUS",
     "TENTATIVE, CONFIRMED or CANCELLED."
    ],
    [
     "END:VEVENT",
     "Required. Ends a single calendar event."
    ],
    [
     "END:VCALENDAR",
     "Required. Ends a calendar object."
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Calendar Systems in JavaScript"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Temporal supports multiple calendar systems",
    "The calendars are based on the Unicode CLDR standard",
    "They are used with the Intl API.",
    "The default is iso8601.",
    "Calendars affect how dates are interpreted and displayed.",
    "Use [u-ca=calendar] to specify a calendar."
   ]
  },
