  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Calendar Systems Explained"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "A calendar system defines how dates are calculated."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Different cultures use different calendars."
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Solar Calendars"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Based on the Earth's orbit around the sun."
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Gregorian",
    "ISO 8601",
    "Persian"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "These calendars track seasons accurately."
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Lunar Calendars"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Based on the phases of the moon."
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Islamic"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Lunar calendars have shorter years."
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Lunisolar Calendars"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Combine solar and lunar cycles."
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Chinese",
    "Hebrew",
    "Dangi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "They adjust months to stay aligned with seasons."
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Era-Based Calendars"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Use eras instead of a continuous year count."
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Japanese",
    "ROC (Taiwan)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Using Calendars in Temporal"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The from() method supports calendars using the [u-ca=calendar] syntax or a calendar\nproperty in objects."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "Temporal.PlainDate.from(\"2026-05-17[u-ca=japanese]\")",
   "caption": "Examples"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "js",
   "text": "Temporal.PlainDate.from({year:2026, month:5, day:17, calendar:\"hebrew\"})",
   "caption": "Examples"
  },
  {
